### 3.2 End-to-end CLI transcripts

`cmd/demo` emits a vector; `cmd/vss` consumes it. All are reproducible.

**Transmission corruption.** Honest dealer of `0x42` (`n=7, k=3`); commitment over correct shares, two shares damaged in transit:

```bash
go run ./cmd/demo corrupt | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"secret":"42","corrupt_indices":[3,6],"classification":"CORRUPT_SHARES","max_unique_e":2}
```

**Dealer equivocation.** Dealer commits to values from two different degree-2 polynomials (`p = 0x11 + 0x22x + 0x33x²`, `q = 0x44 + 0x55x + 0x66x²`):

```bash
go run ./cmd/demo equivocation | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"secret":"11","corrupt_indices":[4,6],"classification":"DEALER_EQUIVOCATION","max_unique_e":2}
```

**Ambiguous.** `n=4, k=2, e=2`, so `2e = 4 ≥ n-k+1 = 3`. Two distinct lines, `p(x)=x` and `q(x)=x+1`, both explain the data:

```bash
go run ./cmd/demo ambiguous | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"classification":"AMBIGUOUS","max_unique_e":1,"ambiguous_polynomials":["0001","0101"]}
```

The reported coefficient strings decode as `0x00 + 0x01·x` and `0x01 + 0x01·x`, exactly `p` and `q`.

**Edge cases and rejection:**

```bash
# k=1 majority vote (0x33 appears 4/5 times)
echo '{"n":5,"k":1,"shares":[{"index":1,"value":"33"},{"index":2,"value":"33"},{"index":3,"value":"99"},{"index":4,"value":"33"},{"index":5,"value":"33"}]}' | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"secret":"33","corrupt_indices":[3],"classification":"CORRUPT_SHARES","max_unique_e":2}

# n=k, all-zero secret
echo '{"n":3,"k":3,"shares":[{"index":1,"value":"00"},{"index":2,"value":"00"},{"index":3,"value":"00"}]}' | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"secret":"00","classification":"VALID","max_unique_e":0}

# non-canonical uppercase hex is rejected, exit status 1
echo '{"n":3,"k":2,"shares":[{"index":1,"value":"0A"},{"index":2,"value":"0b"},{"index":3,"value":"0c"}]}' | go run ./cmd/vss
# {"classification":"ERROR","max_unique_e":0,"error":"non-canonical share \"0A\": must be lowercase hex"}
```

### 3.3 Scale

Gaussian elimination is `O(n·(k+2t)²)` per error-locator degree, sweeping `t` up to the radius. Worst-case `n = 255` on this machine:

| `n` | `k` | `e_max` | decode time |
|-----|-----|---------|-------------|
| 255 | 128 | 63  | 0.42 s |
| 255 | 200 | 27  | 0.21 s |
| 255 | 50  | 102 | 0.45 s |
| 255 | 2   | 126 | 0.40 s |

At the minimal error-locator degree the affine solution space has dimension at most 2 (`k+2t−n ≤ 2`), so the exhaustive `256^d ≤ 65,536` enumeration for ambiguity is cheap.

